{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Surely</b> — the words of the maskil." "And the sense of <b>I have made my heart pure</b> — that my thought is a thought of truth and my faith is pure with the Creator, and for this reason man was created, so that his soul in his lifetime be pure and radiant like the stars." "And the sense of <b>pure</b> my hands — that I did no act of filth and defilement, such as is not fitting to do." "And he mentioned <b>my hands</b> — for most actions are with the hands."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:14.046041805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}